# game/src/ai/behaviours.list — every behaviour the engine has, by code.
#
# ONE system (owner 2026-11-24: "we need them synced taxonomy and engine" · "enforce then"):
# the club's taxonomy of football and this engine are the same list. A behaviour is a
# distinct football thing a player or the team reads or does. Each one has
#
#   1. a tag in the code, on the line above it:      // [behaviour: <code>]
#   2. a line in this file
#   3. a row in the database (game_engine_behaviours) that names its catalogue concept —
#      or says it has none yet, or that it is a fudge.  ⚽ Football → 🧬 Taxonomy shows it.
#
# scripts/check_behaviours.sh runs in the image build beside the determinism lints and
# FAILS the build when 1 and 2 disagree: a tag with no line here, a line here with no tag,
# a code twice here. `make game-deploy` first runs scripts/taxonomy/check_engine_sync.py,
# which fails when 2 and 3 disagree. So a new behaviour ships with all three or not at all:
# add the tag, add the line, add the row by migration (docs/taxonomy-one-system.md).
#
# "pending" after a code = its tag is not in the source yet (the file was being worked on
# when the tags went in); the lint lets it through. Remove the word when the tag lands.
